{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "blkou_l1",
  "notes": "Blackout gameplay causality with direct public switch writes only (keyboard handling and the driver's simulator stay off). The ball rests in the outhole (switch 9); a coin must fire the credit knocker (14) and the credit button must start a game, reset both 3-banks (4, 5) and fire the ball release (1). The jet bumper and kicker scoring switches 22, 21, 23, 44 and 43 must each publish their switch-driven special solenoid 17-21 at once. A 1 rollover and the synthetic flipper buttons 82 and 84 show the lane-change rotation and outputs 45-48. The five green targets are made, then each 3-bank is worked with its three targets held down first and its series switch (28 or 36) closed afterwards, so the run shows which closure the ROM resets the bank on. A ball in the eject hole (40) with BLACKOUT lit must be kicked out by solenoid 6, the outhole drain must count bonus and serve the next ball with solenoid 1, and a single ball roll tilt closure must drop game-on 23. The host moves the ball itself; that movement is not ROM evidence. Run from an NVRAM initialized by one prior empty-NVRAM power-up.",
